PS2Native's change to PCSX2 number 2: FullscreenUI_Settings.cpp includes
<sstream>.

Made on 2026-11-27 for PCSX2 v2.9.198, in the trial of that version, and
carried since PS2Native moved to it, at the maintainer's word (docs/adr/0061
and 0062 in PS2Native's repository). It is PS2Native's own, not PCSX2's:
PCSX2's source as PCSX2 released it is the submodule third_party/pcsx2, which
this is applied to a copy of when PS2Native's runtime is built. Licence:
PCSX2's, GPL-3.0-or-later.

What it changes. pcsx2/ImGui/FullscreenUI_Settings.cpp uses
std::istringstream (lines 1568 and 1616) and does not include <sstream>.
Before v2.9.196 common/StringUtil.h included it for every file that included
that header; v2.9.196 ("Common: Move To and FromChars implementations out of
header") took those includes out. This adds the include, and nothing else.

Why. Without it the file does not compile on Linux here (Ubuntu 22.04's
libstdc++, with LLVM 22.1.3's clang): "implicit instantiation of undefined
template 'std::basic_istringstream<char>'". PCSX2's own Linux builds of
v2.9.198 compile it, most likely with a newer libstdc++, whose headers bring
<sstream> in by another way.

What it does not change: anything a run does. So it is the one kind of change
applied to the tree stock PCSX2 is timed on as well, which would not build on
Linux here without it (cmake/ps2n-pcsx2-patches.cmake reads this line):

Stock PCSX2's tree is built with it too.

--- a/pcsx2/ImGui/FullscreenUI_Settings.cpp
+++ b/pcsx2/ImGui/FullscreenUI_Settings.cpp
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 #include "fmt/format.h"
 
 #include <set>
+#include <sstream>
 
 namespace FullscreenUI
 {
